                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Another in the series of \"Fancy\" games (Fancy being code for \"kinda lame\")...This time it's Fancy Fishing.  When I heard the title, I thought I'd be in a boat with a rod and reel and lures and stuff. Instead I'm on some kind of pedestal underwater with fish all around me and I just shoot them for points.  (so lame).\n\nIt's not 100% trash, but it's not good enough to warrant a thumbs up. If you got this in a bundle then it's probably worth about what you paid for it (meaning like 1/10th of $3.99 or whatever the bundle was). If you bought this with your own money ... why?  I guess it looks entertaining from the screenshots but trust me, this is not something you'll spend time in.\n\nI don't even really have enough to give a list of things I liked or disliked.  It's just like a wave shooter without much cause to feel like there's any danger, and then there's a mode where you fight a boss (shark or whatever) and then you can buy better weapons since otherwise you'll spend a lot of time trying to kill just one fish.\n\nI know you can do better than this game.",
